  "navigationOpen": "WhiteBox\nBeyond DSA\nLearn\nRoadmap\nStart from zero and work through each topic\nLibrary\nCurated resources, tier lists, and problem sets\nGuides\nReal takes worth your time reading\nWhite Room\nMore\nSearch\nCtrl K\nLogin\nSign up\nLog in\n\nBeyond DSA\n\nCore Catalog\nSystem Design\nDomain Knowledge\nResume Reviewer\n\nLearn\n\nRoadmap\nLibrary\nGuides\n\nWhite Room\n\nWhite Room\nWhite Room DSA\nAbout White Room\n\nMore\n\nLeaderboard\nRefer & Earn\nShop\nInterview Intel\nJob Boards\nSandbox\nChangelog\nContributors",
  "searchOpen": "on of your own. It is defined in the judge.\n\nInput format: The first line contains N, the number of operations. Each of the next N lines is one operation. The operation name maps to methods as follows:\n\nADD server_id → add_server(server_id)\nADD server_id v → add_server(server_id, v)\nREMOVE server_id → remove_server(server_id)\nGET chat_id → get_server(chat_id)\nAFFINITY server_id chat_id → record_affinity(server_id, chat_id)\nGET3 chat_id k → get_server_v3(chat_id, k)\nVRAM server_id chat_id → load_to_vram(server_id, chat_id)\nRAM server_id chat_id → load_to_ram(server_id, chat_id)\nGET4 chat_id k → get_server_v4(chat_id, k)\n\nOutput format: For each GET, GET3, or GET4, print the resolved server_id on its own line. All other operations produce no output.\n\nBrowse Interview Intel\nShare your interview round\nSee your resume the way a recruiter does.\n\nSee where your resume lands across seven score bands, with evidence for each score and feedback weighted toward your target role.\n\nWhere you stand\nA score from 0 to 100, from Thin to Alien, with an estimated percentile for your career stage.\nWhat reads as strong\nSeparate scores for problem solving, experience, research, technical depth, projects, and pedigree, each backed by your resume.\nWhat to rewrite first\nThe weakest lines, each with a rewrite you can paste back in.\nReview my resume\nA real report, on a sample resume.\nBuilt on how people actually learn\n\nYou get good at solving problems by solving them, even when reading solutions feels more productive. Here’s what the studies found, and where it shows up in WhiteBox.\n\nActive vs passive\nDSA practice\nInterviews\nPassive learning feels better. Active learning works better.\n\nMost people watch the video solution, feel like they learned it, and make very little progress. The lecture students in this study fell for the same thing: they felt they learned more and scored lower.\n\nActive doesn’t mean struggling alone. Asking Tsuki, the AI chat on every plan, for the minimal hint to unblock yourself instead of the answer is scaffolding in Lev Vygotsky’s Zone of Proximal Development: just enough support to solve a problem slightly beyond what you can do alone.\n\nRead: Is NeetCode / Strivers A2Z bad?\n\nActive class versus a passive lecture\n\n−0.5 SD\nLecture\n+0.5 SD\nTest of learning\n+0.46\nFeeling of learning\n−0.56\n149 students in introductory physics, taught the same material both ways. Deslauriers et al. (2019), PNAS\nHalloween: 27% off\nChoose your WhiteBox plan\n\nEnds in\n5d 03h 15m 42s\n\nAnnual\nMonthly\nFree\n$0\n/mo\n\nEverything WhiteBox has to offer for free.\n\nStart for free\nSee what's inside\n48 original implementation problems in the Core Catalog\n912 curated DSA problems in the algorithm roadmaps\n1,900+ quiz questions across algorithms and domain knowledge\nAlgorithm roadmaps that map out what to learn next\nInterview intel from real candidates, free forever\nDaily quests, streaks, and the global leaderboard\nTsuki AI chat for hints and explanations\n36 in-depth guides and writeups, always free\nProgress that persists across every session\nUltra Premium\n27% off\n$29/mo\n$21\n/mo\n\nRenews at $21/month. Cancel any time.\n\n0.1% of your future salary.\n\nStart 5-day free trial\nSee what's inside\nEverything in Free\nWhite Room: an AI coach that plans your whole prep around your goal\nA roadmap the coach rewrites as you go\nMemory that persists across sessions and brings back your weak spots\nAdaptive DSA practice: a hand of unseen problems picked for your level\nDSA AI coaching and weekly check-ins with shared learner memory\nUnlimited AI resume reviews\nExclusive interview problems from our community members\nA private Discord channel (on request)\nAn Ultra Premium badge and card frame to show it off\n\nFor new Premium subscriptions. Keep the shown rate while your subscription stays active.\n\nOnly want DSA practice? DSA Premium, with Mindsolve, is $9/mo or $79/yr. See DSA Premium\n\nRegional pricing? Message @level5esper on Discord.\n\nWhiteBox\n\nMake the interview a mere formality.\n\n@level5esper\n@meemee.ac\nProduct\nWhite Room\nProblems\nRoadmap\nKnowledge\nLibrary\nCommunity\nInterview Intel\nContributors\nLeaderboard\nTools\nPython Notebooks\nResume Reviewer\nJob Boards\nCompany\nChangelog\nContact\n\n© 2026 WhiteBox. All rights reserved.\n\nPrivacy\nTerms\n✦\n🎃\n✦\nesc\nGo to\nCore Catalog\nAlgorithms roadmap\nWhite Room\nDan ladder\nSaved problems\nDomain knowledge\nLibrary\nGuides\nInterview Intel\nResume review\nLeaderboard\nContest calendar\nCPguessr\nAI-dle\nNotebooks\nChangelog\nPricing\nSettings\n↑\n↓\nto move\n↵\nto open",
